<%#
  The answer, streamed.

  Replaces only the tail of the thread: the rows this answer produced, then
  whatever the run is now waiting on. Everything above is untouched, which is
  the whole point — the transcript the agent was reading stays exactly where it
  was instead of the page repainting under them.

  The tail is computed through the same traversal the page renders from, so a
  streamed thread and a refreshed one cannot disagree.

  locals: scenario, tail, step, parked, results_url, next_url, stop_url,
          back_button, show_cancel, errors, submitted
%>
<%= turbo_stream.replace "runner-card-current" do %>
  <% tail.each do |entry| %>
    <% if entry["kind"] == "group_start" %>
      <%= render "runner/thread_group", entry: entry %>
    <% else %>
      <%= render "runner/thread_row", entry: entry %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <%= render "runner/thread_tail",
        scenario: scenario, step: step, parked: parked, results_url: results_url,
        next_url: next_url, stop_url: stop_url, back_button: back_button,
        show_cancel: show_cancel, errors: errors, submitted: submitted,
        auto_advance: step ? runner_auto_advances?(step) : false %>
<% end %>
